34
00:01:32,910 --> 00:01:37,010
Okay, so it's basically a wrap that is covered in cheese, right?

35
00:01:37,250 --> 00:01:37,810
That's right.

36
00:01:38,270 --> 00:01:41,530
So it has a base of a flour tortilla.

37
00:01:41,770 --> 00:01:43,690
So a tortilla is like a wrap, as you said.

38
00:01:43,890 --> 00:01:45,960
Let's consider it as flat bread.

39
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:47,760
Very thin.

40
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:48,760
Very thin.

41
00:01:48,760 --> 00:01:50,820
And it rolls up and it's covered with cheese and inside it has chicken.

42
00:01:51,280 --> 00:01:51,780
Very, very good.

43
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:52,460
That's right.

44
00:01:53,280 --> 00:02:00,800
So this is the beginning, you're going to hear me say the American pronunciation, enchilada, and you're going to hear Marco say a more appropriate.

45
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:03,380
A little bit with a more Hispanic accent to it.

46
00:02:03,640 --> 00:02:03,800
That's right.

47
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:06,500
So the second one we've got is guacamole.

48
00:02:06,980 --> 00:02:07,460
Guacamole.

49
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:07,920
That's right.

50
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:11,760
We say guacamole and this is from the avocado fruit.

51
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:12,700
That's right.

52
00:02:13,560 --> 00:02:15,680
Avocados are green fruits.

53
00:02:15,680 --> 00:02:16,680
They have a skin.

54
00:02:16,920 --> 00:02:21,840
So you take the skin off and you usually mix guacamole with other ingredients.

55
00:02:22,420 --> 00:02:22,540
Right.

56
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:24,380
A little bit of lemon, onion, tomato.

57
00:02:24,760 --> 00:02:25,340
Maybe a little spice.

58
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:26,480
Really good stuff.

59
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:32,890
So yeah, it comes from that fruit that you said and it's kind of like a paste, right?

60
00:02:32,960 --> 00:02:36,160
Yeah, it's something that we often use as a dip.

61
00:02:36,160 --> 00:02:41,010
So I can dip my potato chips or my tortilla chips in it or I can use it as a sauce.

62
00:02:41,450 --> 00:02:41,830
All right.

63
00:02:41,990 --> 00:02:42,450
Very good.

64
00:02:43,050 --> 00:02:50,130
And our next and probably one of the most popular dishes in the Mexican cuisine world is a beef burrito.

65
00:02:50,610 --> 00:02:51,010
Burrito.

66
00:02:51,370 --> 00:02:52,970
So a burrito is another kind of wrap.

67
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:58,560
We have a tortilla like you said earlier and inside there are many different things.

68
00:02:58,900 --> 00:03:04,780
So usually some rice and some beans and some meat, maybe beef or chicken.

69
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:05,640
That's right.

70
00:03:05,960 --> 00:03:10,540
So consider it kind of like a sandwich more or less.

71
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:12,620
But in a blanket instead of in bread.

72
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:13,280
Exactly.

73
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:14,060
In a blanket.

74
00:03:14,700 --> 00:03:17,280
And then also we have cheese quesadillas.

75
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:22,960
Now also these are made from the same blanket of tortilla.

76
00:03:23,320 --> 00:03:23,680
That's right.

77
00:03:23,800 --> 00:03:35,180
So this thin tortilla, this flour tortilla is put on top and on bottom and inside you have some cheese, some melted cheese or other times you can have cheese and chicken.

78
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:39,480
And usually you find it's a circle but it's cut into four pieces.

79
00:03:39,480 --> 00:03:41,060
So it looks like pieces of a pie.

80
00:03:41,340 --> 00:03:41,700
That's right.

81
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:50,480
And what you do is you heat it up in a pan so the cheese inside melts and it's very, very delicious.

82
00:03:50,960 --> 00:03:51,380
It is.

83
00:03:51,560 --> 00:03:54,580
And sometimes you have this with a side of jalapeno.

84
00:03:55,100 --> 00:03:55,560
Okay.

85
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:58,780
This is some type of vegetable I would guess.

86
00:03:59,120 --> 00:03:59,380
It's a pepper.

87
00:04:00,120 --> 00:04:01,120
It's a pepper.

88
00:04:01,120 --> 00:04:02,120
Right.

89
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:06,320
So this is a very, very spicy pepper that people often use to make things taste hot.

90
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:06,460
That's right.

91
00:04:07,320 --> 00:04:07,580
So you can see them.

92
00:04:08,320 --> 00:04:11,360
They're usually green and they're very, very spicy.

93
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:14,800
So if you bite into one, it'll burn your mouth.

94
00:04:14,800 --> 00:04:15,800
It will.

95
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:18,080
And sometimes people like to put these on our next dish.

96
00:04:18,520 --> 00:04:19,240
