111
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:19,260
Hello, sir.

112
00:05:19,440 --> 00:05:21,000
Welcome to Pistolero Restaurant.

113
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:22,480
May I take your order?

114
00:05:22,500 --> 00:05:26,820
Yes, I would like the chicken cheese enchiladas with a side of guacamole.

115
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:29,020
Sorry, sir, but we ran out of chicken.

116
00:05:29,640 --> 00:05:32,740
May I suggest our delicious beef burritos or cheese quesadillas?

117
00:05:33,360 --> 00:05:36,160
Both include a side of guacamole and jalapenos.

118
00:05:36,420 --> 00:05:37,800
Sure, I'll have the burrito.

119
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:39,160
Do you have nachos?

120
00:05:39,400 --> 00:05:40,760
Of course, sir.

121
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:42,680
Our nachos come with melted cheese and chili.

122
00:05:43,300 --> 00:05:43,920
Sounds good.

123
00:05:44,420 --> 00:05:45,520
Would you like anything to drink?

124
00:05:46,100 --> 00:05:47,520
Sure, I'll have a Corona.

125
00:05:48,880 --> 00:05:55,800
All right, so Marco, today we have only three things to talk about in Fluency Builder.

126
00:05:55,800 --> 00:05:58,440
The first one is something that the waiter said to the customer.

127
00:05:58,760 --> 00:06:00,960
It was to run out of.

128
00:06:00,960 --> 00:06:01,960
That's right.

129
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:06,210
He wanted some chicken cheese enchiladas, but unfortunately they ran out of chicken.

130
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:09,090
So the phrasal verb here is to run out of.

131
00:06:09,350 --> 00:06:11,010
That's right, and we heard the past tense.

132
00:06:11,350 --> 00:06:13,430
So unfortunately, we ran out of chicken.

133
00:06:13,650 --> 00:06:17,010
This means that we no longer have chicken.

134
00:06:17,330 --> 00:06:18,670
We sold all of the chicken.

135
00:06:18,950 --> 00:06:19,350
That's right.

136
00:06:19,830 --> 00:06:26,350
So for example, if you're in your car and all of a sudden you run out of gasoline, it means your car will stop running.

137
00:06:26,630 --> 00:06:27,970
That's very bad situation.

138
00:06:28,600 --> 00:06:32,160
So to run out of means to not have any more.

139
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:32,460
That's right.

140
00:06:33,160 --> 00:06:34,020
So you ran out of money.

141
00:06:34,440 --> 00:06:35,280
Maybe you have no more money.

142
00:06:35,440 --> 00:06:37,640
That's another bad situation.

143
00:06:37,640 --> 00:06:42,800
So instead he ordered a burrito that included a side of guacamole and jalapenos.

144
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:49,120
Okay, so the reason we included this is because it's important to remember this as a phrase, a side of.

145
00:06:49,380 --> 00:06:49,700
That's right.

146
00:06:49,780 --> 00:06:56,580
So this burrito comes with a side of guacamole or this burrito has a side of beans.

147
00:06:57,640 --> 00:07:01,640
So a side of means a small portion, a little bit.

148
00:07:01,640 --> 00:07:01,820
That's right.

149
00:07:02,640 --> 00:07:09,760
So the important part of a side of is that it doesn't come in the dish or inside the burrito let's say.

150
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:12,080
It just comes separately on a separate little plate.

151
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:15,380
Or it can come next to the main dish.

152
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:23,560
So if the main dish is tacos, you can say I want tacos with a side of black beans.

153
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:25,430
You would get the black beans in a little bowl next to you.

154
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,530
But that's not the main thing.

155
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:28,320
Exactly, exactly.

156
00:07:28,350 --> 00:07:29,610
So a side of.

157
00:07:29,610 --> 00:07:36,850
Now for our last phrase, when we talked about the nachos, they came with melted cheese and chili.

158
00:07:36,850 --> 00:07:40,780
So what do we mean by they come with melted cheese and chili?

159
00:07:41,140 --> 00:07:46,020
Okay, so this verb to come with means that they have as a part of the dish.

160
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:47,800
So this is not a side.

161
00:07:48,920 --> 00:07:51,280
Not like before when we were talking about a side of.

162
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:58,100
This means that in the case of nachos, the nachos have on them, on top, cheese and chili.

163
00:07:58,380 --> 00:07:58,960
That's right.

164
00:07:59,220 --> 00:08:08,610
So sometimes if you go to McDonald's and you buy a meal, you get a burger and the burger comes with French fries and a Coke included in the meal.

165
00:08:08,850 --> 00:08:13,490
Or you can say, unfortunately, this meal does not come with a drink.

166
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,120
So you have to order the drink extra.

167
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:16,410
That's right.

168
00:08:17,120 --> 00:08:18,790
Okay, so a lot of great stuff.

